        "The public participant list, off on every event until the club switches it on, shows only the name (or display name) and club of those who ticked “I want to appear on the participants & results list” when registering (and the race number of the confirmed and, where they chose it, their Strava and Instagram — below), for at most {{publicListPeriod}} after the event, after which the list closes by itself — consent, art. 6(1)(a) GDPR, withdrawn at any time from “My registrations”, or from the link in your confirmation email; no tick, no listing.",
        "Beside each name the list shows where the registration stands — {{participantListStates}}. It holds the confirmed participants, those who confirmed their address and have not yet signed the declaration, and those on the waiting list, in its order, without a numbered place. A registration with an unconfirmed address, or cancelled, expired or erased, does not appear; confirmed participants without the tick are only counted. If you registered under an older version of this notice, which did not describe the states, you appear on the list, as before, only once your place is confirmed.",
        "Beside the name of each confirmed participant the list also shows the {{participantListNumbers}} — the one they wear in the race. A confirmed participant who has no number yet appears without one. Those whose place is not confirmed yet, those on the waiting list and those not shown by name have no number on the list. The number is part of your listing: you withdraw it with the listing.",
        "Beside your name, the list also shows the Strava link and the Instagram username you gave on the form, each linked to your profile, only if you also ticked {{participantListSocials}} — a separate consent (art. 6(1)(a) GDPR) that changes nothing else about your registration. Without the tick, or if you are not on the list, they do not appear. For a minor they never appear, because we keep none. You withdraw it at any time from “My registrations”, by deleting your Strava and Instagram or by leaving the list; they leave the list at once.",
        "A race's results ({{results}} on the event's page) appear only after the race, only for that race, and only if one of the club's administrators publishes them. For each runner they show the place (overall, by sex and in their category), the race number, the time, whether they finished, dropped out, did not start or were disqualified, and the category — the sex and age group on the day of the race. The club types the times, from the race's timing.",
        "The name (or display name) appears in the results only for those who ticked “I want to appear on the participants & results list” when registering — one tick for the list and the results, withdrawn the same way, from “My registrations” or from the link in your confirmation email, and the name then leaves the results too (consent, art. 6(1)(a) GDPR). Everyone else appears as “Participant #race number”, with place, time and category but no name (legitimate interest, art. 6(1)(f) GDPR: showing how the race went). A runner who did not register and whose time the organizers entered by hand appears by name only if they told the organizers they want to (for a minor, the parent or guardian tells them); otherwise they appear as “Participant #race number”. The organizers record the agreement in the log, with who recorded it and when. The runner (for a minor, the parent or guardian) can withdraw the agreement at any time by writing to us, and the name then leaves the results (consent, art. 6(1)(a) GDPR). If you registered under an older version of this notice, which did not describe the results, you appear in them only by number, as “Participant #race number”, even if you ticked. The results close by themselves with the public list, within the same period. In our database, the results stay as long as we keep the race's registrations (section 7); the name the club typed for a runner who did not register stays no longer.",
        "The {{rsvp}} answer on the page of an event that needs no registration (a group run, for example) shows publicly how many said they are coming and, row by row, the name only of those who ticked “I want my name to show”; everyone else is only counted, with no name. Without the tick nothing about you appears but the total. Basis for the name: your consent (art. 6(1)(a) GDPR), which you can withdraw at any time with the “I'm not coming any more” link in the email you received or by writing to <CONTACT EMAIL>. An answer is not a registration: it holds no place and signs no declaration.",
        "Photographs and video from events, published in the gallery and on the club's channels: legitimate interest (art. 6(1)(f) GDPR) — showing the club's events; public place, no names, no EXIF. A portrait is published only with your agreement (Romanian Civil Code, art. 73–75). Tell us which and we take it down within a month, no reason needed.",
        "The site's {{teamPage}} page introduces the people in the club's team and the volunteers who agreed to appear: their name, what they do for the club, a few words about them, a photograph and, if they wish, a link to a public profile of theirs. Basis: each person's consent (art. 6(1)(a) GDPR; Romanian Civil Code, art. 73–75), which they may withdraw at any time by writing to us: their card is taken off the site without delay and without asking for a reason, and the photograph is deleted.",
