        "For volunteers and organisers with access to the platform we keep name, email address and role, who did what on the platform, and the name of whoever recorded a paper declaration. Zitadel holds the sign-in account; a session lasts 30 days. Basis: our legitimate interest in knowing who has access and who acted (art. 6(1)(f) and art. 5(2) GDPR). When access is withdrawn we delete the account on the platform, and the Zitadel one on request; the log stays at most three years.",
        "The club's members may receive an account with which they enter the members' area of the site. For them we keep name, email address, the member role, preferred language, the date of the first sign-in and the membership level the club gives them, if it gives one (only the administrators see it); we email them the invitation, and Zitadel holds the sign-in account, as for the team, with the same 30-day session. The members' area shows only the text the club writes for its members and the published events; it shows no other member's data and gives no access to running the site. Basis: the club's legitimate interest in offering its members what it promised them (art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). A member may ask us at any time to delete their account by writing to us; we also delete it when they are no longer a member, and the Zitadel one on request.",
